    {
        "content": "<p>Are the PR's you're mentioning assigned to someone? Do they appear in the \"PR reviews\" stream so that someone can take care of them?</p>",
        "id": 578598308,
        "sender_full_name": "Filippo A. E. Nuccio",
        "timestamp": 1773224408
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The first three of Winston's PRs each have an assignee now, and have been reviewed in the past two days.</p>",
        "id": 578601462,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1773225250
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There is no particular reason for the delay, merely not enough reviewers with capacity (until now).</p>",
        "id": 578601659,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1773225297
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Great news! <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"416472\">@Winston Yin (尹維晨)</span> how about this for the exponential map (of a Lie group)? Also I got as far as defining the fundamental vector field. I think I need 1-forms to go further but I can fake these as sections of the cotangent bundle.</p>\n<p><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/9fYtR2voX5HaAufeG3Ei8uJW/PastedText.txt\">PastedText.txt</a></p>\n<p>Maybe I should make this into a PR so that it's easier to look at from Tulip.</p>",
        "id": 578876898,
        "sender_full_name": "Dominic Steinitz",
        "timestamp": 1773309515
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The text file you posted has font conversion problems. Using <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib/wiki/Code-in-backticks\">#backticks</a> or opening a PR both is much more readable.</p>",
        "id": 578879410,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1773310229
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Have you seen <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=isMIntegralCurveAt_eventuallyEq_of_contMDiffAt%3F#doc\">docs#isMIntegralCurveAt_eventuallyEq_of_contMDiffAt?</a> This is a much more conceptual statement than <code>IsMIntegralCurve.unique_global</code> in your file.</p>",
        "id": 578880918,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1773310646
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>exists_global</code> should use the results in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/26395\">#26395</a>, in the medium term (and wait on that PR being merged, before it can be merged into mathlib).</p>",
        "id": 578881364,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1773310763
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Most other lemmas look like useful statements to me. (I haven't checked carefully how much they should also be generalised.)</p>",
        "id": 578881543,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1773310807
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My general impression is that your proofs can be shortened and cleaned up quite a bit.</p>",
        "id": 578881688,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1773310840
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And a general comment, from discussions with <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"260507\">@Heather Macbeth</span> last week: it's not clear if using integral curves all the time is the best API, or we should mostly talk about flows (and the maximal flow) of a vector field instead. Thus, if an integral curves result you're proving really follows from a result about flows, you should prove the flows result first.</p>",
        "id": 578881926,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1773310911
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think Tulip forced me to paste a file but anyway here is a draft PR which should be easier to read: <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36529\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36529</a></p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"634338\">@Michael Rothgang</span> thanks for your comments - I am tied up with other things for the next few days. The proofs were meant as nothing more than to capture my thinking. Since my goal is to define a connection 1-form I think I am going to need 1-forms but as I said I think I can fake those for now and get my ducks in a row and have something available for discussion.</p>\n<p>Are flows in Mathlib yet? I thought <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"416472\">@Winston Yin (尹維晨)</span>'s PRs just dealt with integral curves - oh wait there is</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- Existence of local flows for a $C^1$ vector field at interior points of a $C^1$ manifold. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exists_mem_nhds_isMIntegralCurveOn_Ioo_of_contMDiffAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CompleteSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ContMDiffAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tangent</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TangentBundle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x₀</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsInteriorPoint</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x₀</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝓝</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x₀</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t₀</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">IsMIntegralCurveOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·⟩</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Ioo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×ˢ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ioo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I will think more about flows when I get some time.</p>",
        "id": 578913872,
        "sender_full_name": "Dominic Steinitz",
        "timestamp": 1773320040
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here's a proof assuming the smooth dependence of ODE solutions on parameters (Lee, <em>Introduction to Smooth Manifolds</em>, Theorem 9.12), which is currently missing(?) from Mathlib:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37932\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37932</a></p>\n<p>BTW the proofs I found in some of the more popular expositions resisted my attempts at formalisation. Luckily I found Eckhard Meinrenken's lecture notes. I can't prove that the other expositions are wrong but I am starting to think they are suspect.</p>\n<p>Only finite dimensions though.</p>",
        "id": 584951667,
        "sender_full_name": "Dominic Steinitz",
        "timestamp": 1775913401
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I just realised I had better change the name of the file and possibly its location but at least it now exists.</p>",
        "id": 584951778,
        "sender_full_name": "Dominic Steinitz",
        "timestamp": 1775913483
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/34288\">#34288</a> proves smooth dependence on initial conditions --- so indeed, mathlib doesn't have this yet.</p>",
        "id": 585015886,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1775979948
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"634338\">Michael Rothgang</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Lie.20group.20exponential.20map/near/585015886\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/34288\">#34288</a> proves smooth dependence on initial conditions --- so indeed, mathlib doesn't have this yet.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Thanks for the pointer - I was already aware of this and it is great and I wish it would make its way into Mathlib but it only covers Banach spaces and not manifolds and is only C1 (that is not meant to sound negative and I will have a think about how to fill in the gap).</p>",
        "id": 585052973,
        "sender_full_name": "Dominic Steinitz",
        "timestamp": 1776015850
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My understanding is that Winston is also thinking about the smooth case, and that deducing the manifold case from the Banach case is probably easier than the normed space case.</p>",
        "id": 585065708,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1776027682
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(I also hope both can progress!)</p>",
        "id": 585065760,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1776027719
    }
]